      $( Lemma for ~ prmrec .  Here we show the inequality ` N / 2 < # M ` by
         decomposing the set ` ( 1 ... N ) ` into the disjoint union of the set
         ` M ` of those numbers that are not divisible by any "large" primes
         (above ` K ` ) and the indexed union over ` K < k ` of the numbers
         ` W `` k ` that divide the prime ` k ` .  By ~ prmreclem4 the second
         of these has size less than ` N ` times the prime reciprocal series,
         which is less than ` 1 / 2 ` by assumption, we find that the
         complementary part ` M ` must be at least ` N / 2 ` large.
         (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Aug-2014.) $)
